    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18552" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fŏrentum</span></b>  (in some MSS. of Horace <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fĕrentum</span></b> ),
		i, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small town in Apulia</i>, now <i>Forenza</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 9, 20,
				9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3, 4, 16</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fŏrentāni</span></b> ,
			ōrum, <i>its inhabitants</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 11, 16, § 105</span></i>.</div>
